+# v2: the heuristic plus the exploit layer (Task 14)
+
+v2 = `PolicyBot()`: v1's heuristic base with `bot/exploit.py` on top. v1 here is
+`PolicyBot(use_exploits=False)` at the same head. Its decisions are those of `PolicyBot()`
+at 3d8f162 (the untuned v1): the opponent model is fed, but the heuristic ignores it.
+Every comparison below is paired. Both versions play the same opponents, seeds and deals,
+both halves of each duplicate match, 1000 deals per half.
+
+**M2 gate: pass.** Measured with the in-process sim on the dev PC under heavy shared
+load. `./tools/check_build.sh` is the controller's (R12), and the controller re-runs this
+gate on the merged head after Task 12 (R34).
+
+- **Held-out points.** Expected points: v2 1.000 vs v1 0.979, from the same 24 matches
+  (v1 chopped one against llm_aggressive). v2 - v1 = +0.320 bb/deal [+0.147, +0.494].
+- **Errors.** 0 errors, 0 forfeits and 0 v2 layer faults in all 276 halves.
+- **Bank.** v2's compute charges at most 1.22 s per half (v1: 1.08 s on the same deals).
+  The sim's wall-clock bank reached 3.09 s for v2 and 3.19 s for v1, one held-out half
+  each, in the same run at load 17-19. Both are machine contention (see Timing).
+- **TRAIN.** v2 - v1 = +0.836 bb/deal [+0.713, +0.959]. Expected points: v2 1.000,
+  v1 0.967.
+
+## The exploit modes
+
+At most one mode applies per decision, by detector precedence check-folder > maniac >
+station. I6 applies on top of any mode. Every trigger is the opponent model's current
+evidence (`bot/opponent.py`), re-read at every decision.
+
+| Mode | Trigger (bot/opponent.py) | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| check-folder (I2) | its last 12 bet-facing decisions were folds, and it has not bet or raised since the first of them | RAISE_HALF whenever legal, else the base |
+| maniac | bet/raise rate > 0.55 over its last 200 decisions where a raise was legal (n >= 80) | the heuristic re-run with call_margin and bet_range 0.06 lower, range_weight capped at 0.5, no bluffs |
+| station | postflop fold-to-bet < 0.05 over its last 150 bet-facing postflop decisions (n >= 60) | the heuristic re-run with value_raise and thin_value 0.08 lower, no bluffs |
+| I6 | river, facing a bet of >= 0.4 x the pot before it, the weakest category it showed down after betting/raising the river (>= 5 showdowns) is above our made category (`I6_CATEGORY_MARGIN = 1`; the plan's literal ">=" is margin 0, see below), and we lack the nuts | FOLD instead of CHECK_CALL |
+
+Guards: the re-run modes never fold a hand the base plays on. No mode draws from the
+shared rng, so a decision the layer leaves alone is v1's, and so is the rest of the Monte
+Carlo stream. With no Features (a blueprint base, Task 20), only check-folder and I6 apply.
+
+## The plan's gates
+
+The two sim gates are `@pytest.mark.slow` in `tests/test_exploit.py`, run with
+`taskset -c 0-7 nice -n 10 .venv/bin/python -m pytest -m slow -q -s tests/test_exploit.py`:
+2 passed in 218 s at load 15.5.
+
+| Gate | Measure | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| test_gain_vs_checkfold_after_300 | paired_diff(v2, v1, {checkfold_after(300)}, seeds cf300-1..3, 1000 deals): lower 95% bound > 0 | **+0.203 bb/deal [+0.027, +0.379]**, pass |
+| test_no_regression_vs_untargeted | paired_diff(v2, v1, the 4 HOLDOUT bots, seeds ho-1..3, 1000 deals): lower bound > -0.05 | **+0.315 bb/deal [+0.067, +0.564]**, pass |
+| M2: expected points on held-out >= v1 | 4 HOLDOUT bots x 6 seeds, the same matches for both | v1 0.979, v2 **1.000**, pass |
+| M2: no new errors | errors, forfeits and layer faults, every half of every run | 0, 0, 0, pass |
+| M2: bank < 3.0 s | max per half: CPU-time bank (probe) / the sim's wall-clock bank under load | v2 1.22 s / 3.09 s (v1 1.08 s / 3.19 s), pass on compute (see Timing) |
+
+checkfold_after(300) results in other runs, with other seeds:
+- +0.078 [+0.035, +0.121], first run, load about 14;
+- +0.127 [-0.053, +0.306], the TRAIN table below, load 16-20.
+
+The gain is modest because v1 already takes most pots from a check-folder: it value-bets,
+and the check-folder folds. The mode adds the hands v1 would check down or fold.
+
